meta {
  name: invitations
  seq: 9
}

docs {
  The full invitation lifecycle: invite, list, get, accept, reinvite,
  revoke. Every request except accept requires an admin token; accept
  requires none, by design — see accept-invitation.bru.

  No department_id is set on the invitations this folder creates. The org
  folder runs before this one and deletes the department it created, so
  referencing it here would fail with REFERENCE_CONFLICT once the
  collection has run past org/delete-department.

  create-invitation and reinvite-invitation both answer with a one-time
  token field, alongside the invitation — see CreatedInvitation in
  api/openapi.yaml for why the API hands it back directly rather than only
  emailing it. accept-invitation is what makes that token real: it is the
  only way this collection can exercise the accept endpoint at all, since
  nothing here has a mailbox to read.
}
